The Cortex-M4F STM32F407VG MCU contains an advanced floating-point unit (FPU) that enables high-performance, single-precision (FP32) and double-precision (FP64) floating-point calculations. This FPU is designed to work seamlessly with the ARM Cortex-M4 CPU core, allowing for efficient mixed-mode C/C++ programming with both fixed-point and floating-point data types.

How it Works:

The FPU operates by performing arithmetic operations on floating-point numbers using specialized hardware circuits. These circuits execute instructions such as addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, square root, and trigonometric functions much faster than software implementations using fixed-point arithmetic.

The FPU is integrated into the Cortex-M4F CPU core and can be accessed through dedicated registers and instructions. It supports both IEEE 754-2008 single-precision (32 bits) and double-precision (64 bits) formats.

How to Use it:

To use the FPU, you must enable it in the device's reset or initialization code. By default, the FPU is disabled to reduce power consumption when not needed. Once enabled, you can access the FPU through dedicated registers and instructions.

