\begin{poem}[12pt]
\begin{flushleft}
\textbf{Friends, Once Near, Now Far}
\end{flushleft}

\begin{enumerate}
\item Friends, once near, now far,
Sorrow fills the empty space they leave behind;
Memories forgotten, left to scar,
In their wake, we struggle to find.

\item But how can we forget the smiles,
The laughter we shared with such delight?
How can we ignore the warmth that piles,
And leaves us feeling so out of sight?

\item The heart remembers, even when the mind,
Forgotten are the times we held so dear;
The memories persist, though hard to find,
A bittersweet reminder, we both hold near.

\item In this sea of melancholy, we seek solace,
Hoping to find some peace within our hearts;
Forgetting not the joys that filled our days,
But remembering those who made them start.

\item Though time has passed and distance grown,
Our love for one another never wanes;
It grows stronger as the years roll on,
An unbreakable bond, forever etched in grains.

\item So let us honor those who came before,
Whose memory lingers like the morning dew;
May our love for them forevermore,
Guide us through the sorrows, and help us pull through.
\end{enumerate}
\end{poem}

