```json
"permissions": ["tabs", "activeTab", "http://*/*", "https://*/*"]
```

4. Define the background script in your `background.js` file. This script will be executed when the browser loads the extension, and it's where you can implement the logic to inject scripts into specific web pages. Here's an example:

```javascript
