Java program code to calculate the duration between two dates while considering the time zones:

```java
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.ZoneId;
import java.time.ZonedDateTime;

public class DateDurationCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Set the time zones for both dates
        ZonedDateTime startTime = ZonedDateTime.of(2022, 1, 1, 10, 0, 0, 0, ZoneId.of("Europe/London"));
        ZonedDateTime endTime = ZonedDateTime.of(2022, 1, 1, 15, 30, 0, 0, ZoneId.of("America/New_York"));

        // Convert both dates to the same time zone to avoid issues with daylight saving time differences
        ZoneId londonTimeZone = ZoneId.of("Europe/London");
        ZoneId newYorkTimeZone = ZoneId.of("America/New_York");
        ZoneId commonTimeZone = ZoneId.systemDefault().normalized();
        startTime = startTime.withZoneSameInstant(commonTimeZone);
        endTime = endTime.withZoneSameInstant(commonTimeZone);

        // Calculate the duration between the two dates
        Duration duration = Duration.between(startTime, endTime);

        // Display the result
        System.out.println("Duration: " + duration);
    }
}
```

